# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

REGIONAL GAZETTE

JOMBANG REGENCY YEAR 2008

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF JOMBANG REGENCY

NUMBER 14 YEAR 2008

CONCERNING

SERIES E NUMBER 14

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF JOMBANG,

Considering:

a. that in order to optimize efforts directed towards reducing the number of acts of violence against women and children, it is deemed necessary to improve the provision of protection services for women and children victims of violence;
b. that to achieve the purpose of consideration letter a, it is deemed necessary to regulate the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence by setting forth its provisions in a Regional Regulation.

In View of:

1. Law Number 4 Year 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3143);
2. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);
3. Law Number 23 Year 1992 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1992 Number 100);
4. Law Number 20 Year 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
5. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
6. Law Number 1 Year 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
7. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 10 Year 2004 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4389);
9. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
10. Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended for the second time by Law Number 12 Year 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2005 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence;
12. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 36 Year 1990 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Rights of the Child;
13. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 88 Year 2002 concerning National Action Plan (RAN) for the Elimination of Trafficking in Women and Children;
14. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 61 Year 2003 concerning National Action Plan for Human Rights of Indonesia 1998-2003.

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF JOMBANG REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF JOMBANG

DECIDES:

To Enact: REGIONAL REGULATION OF JOMBANG REGENCY CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

# CHAPTER I

## GENERAL PROVISIONS

#### Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:
1. Region is Jombang Regency;
2. Regional Government is the Regent and regional apparatus as elements of regional government administration;
3. Regent is the Regent of Jombang;
4. Regional House of Representatives hereinafter referred to as DPRD is the regional people's representative institution as an element of regional government administration;
5. Regional Government Administration is the implementation of government affairs by the Regional Government and DPRD according to the principles of Autonomy and co-administration with the principle of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia as referred to in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
6. Agency is a Regional Work Unit whose main duties and functions include the fields of social affairs, women's empowerment and child protection;
7. Child is a person who has not reached 18 years of age, including those in the womb;
8. Violence is any act that results in or may result in misery or suffering to the victim;
9. Physical violence is any act that causes pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death;
10. Psychological violence is an act that causes fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person:
11. Sexual violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, coercion of sexual relations in an unnatural or unwanted manner against another person whether for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes;
12. Victim is a Woman and Child who experiences misery and or suffering as a result of violence;
13. Protection is all efforts aimed at providing a sense of security to victims either temporarily or based on a Court decision;
14. Service is an action that must be immediately taken for victims when seeing, hearing and reasonably suspected that violence against victims will, is or has occurred;
15. Companion is a person or representative of an institution who has the expertise to provide assistance to victims to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims of violence;
16. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children hereinafter referred to as P2T-P2A is a service provider institution based in a Hospital for victims of violence, especially women and children, which is managed jointly by the regional government and the community incorporated in a Team carried out in a cross-functional and cross-sectoral manner in the form of medical services (including medico-legal), psycho-social and legal services;
17. Safe house is a temporary residence used to provide protection to victims;
18. Community is individuals, individuals, families, groups, communities and social organizations;
19. Family is the smallest unit in society consisting of husband and wife, or husband, wife and their children, or father and his children, and mother and her children;
20. Household is family members and relatives (a person who has a blood relationship with family members) and non-relatives, who live and eat from one kitchen and reside in one house.

# CHAPTER II

## PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

#### Article 2

The principles of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence are:
1. Respect for the rights of victims;
2. Justice and gender equality;
3. Non-discrimination;
4. Best interests of victims.

#### Article 3

The purpose of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence is to provide protection and services to women and children victims of violence based on gender and the best interests of women and children.
